+---
+id: dl-003-invalid-input-is-rejected-with-an-invalid-input-error-before-any-change
+type: decision-log
+title: "Invalid input is rejected with an invalid-input error before any change"
+status: pending
+---
+
+<!-- decision-log body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold verbatim; `memory submit` replaces
+     these placeholder comments with real content and fills the required frontmatter fields. -->
+
+## Context
+Screens pass raw user input to the list. Invalid titles, priorities and tags must be rejected with a clear
+error, and nothing may change. Domain code never throws (r4).
+
+## Decision
+A new `TodoErrorCode`, `invalid-input`, returned as a `Result` by `add`, `rename` and `tag`. Validators
+(`validateTitle`, `validatePriority`, `validateTag`) live in `src/domain/task.ts` and run before any state
+change. Titles are checked after trimming (max 120); tags are not trimmed, and any whitespace rejects them.
+The priority is checked at runtime because callers may bypass the types. `untag` is not validated.
+
+## Consequences
+Callers must handle the new code. A rejected `add` does not consume a task id. `createTask`, `renameTask`
+and `addTag` now return a `Result`.
